---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About Us | PAC SAFA">
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="relative h-[55vh] md:h-[65vh]">
    <img
      src="/images/spread.webp"
      alt="PAC SAFA About"
      class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 h-full flex items-center justify-center">
      <h1 class="text-white text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-center">
        About PAC SAFA
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

      <!-- BRAND STORY -->
      <p class="text-sm tracking-wide text-neutral-700 mb-3">OUR STORY</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold mb-6">
        Built from consistency - not hype.
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 leading-7">
        <p>
          PAC SAFA started from a simple frustration: spending $15–20 on small 30ml beard oils that never felt quite right. I wanted a cleaner, better-balanced blend — something lightweight, effective, and affordable enough to use consistently.
        </p>

        <p>
          So I started mixing my own oils. Adjusting ratios. Testing textures. Finding the right absorption and finish. Over time, friends kept asking what I was using — and that’s when PAC SAFA was born.
        </p>

        <p>
          What began as a personal routine became a refined formula designed for everyday use.
        </p>

        <p class="font-medium">
          Proudly made in Vancouver, BC 🇨🇦
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- HOW TO USE -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-neutral-900">
          How to Use
        </h3>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-700 leading-7">
          <p>
            For best results, apply after showering while your hair is still slightly damp.
          </p>

          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>Massage a small amount into the scalp and hair.</li>
            <li>Focus on thinning areas or dry ends.</li>
            <li>Use 3 times per week for consistency.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Start with less than you think you need — you can always add more.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- INGREDIENT TRANSPARENCY -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-neutral-900">
          Ingredient Transparency
        </h3>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-neutral-700 leading-7">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-1">Jojoba Oil</h4>
            <p>
              A lightweight oil that closely mimics the scalp’s natural sebum. Helps moisturize without clogging pores or leaving heavy residue.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-1">Castor Oil</h4>
            <p>
              Rich and nourishing, traditionally used to support the appearance of thicker, fuller-looking hair and help seal in moisture.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-1">Peppermint Essential Oil</h4>
            <p>
              Provides a refreshing cooling sensation and helps stimulate the scalp, supporting circulation and a healthier-looking environment for hair growth.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- HAIR HEALTH GUIDANCE -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-neutral-900">
          Hair Health & Longevity
        </h3>

        <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 leading-7">
          <p>
            Healthy hair isn’t just about what you apply — it’s about habits.
          </p>

          <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Avoid harsh ingredients</h4>
          <p>
            Many common shampoos contain aggressive surfactants that can dry the scalp and weaken hair over time.
            Try to avoid:
          </p>

          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>Sodium Lauryl Sulfate (SLS)</li>
            <li>Sodium Laureth Sulfate (SLES)</li>
            <li>High-alcohol styling products</li>
            <li>Heavy synthetic fragrance blends</li>
          </ul>

          <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Manage stress</h4>
          <p>
            Chronic stress can disrupt the hair growth cycle and contribute to shedding. Prioritize sleep, exercise, and recovery — your hair reflects your overall health.
          </p>

          <h4 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Consistency over intensity</h4>
          <p>
            Gentle care, scalp stimulation, and a steady routine will always outperform aggressive treatments.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CONTACT -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-neutral-900">
          Contact
        </h3>

        <div class="space-y-3 text-neutral-700">
          <p>Based in Vancouver, BC 🇨🇦</p>
          <p>
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:info@pacsafa.ca" class="underline hover:text-neutral-900">
              info@pacsafa.ca
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>